{
  "about": "The exhaustive allow-list of permitted spine column types (foundation/04, decision 017). This enumeration IS the definition of what may sit on the spine, since 'readable-content type' was never defined, so the boundary is a list, not a description. Every entry is a standing permission, so the list is minimal: exactly the purpose-built domains from 0003-spine-core, each carrying its correlation reasoning in that migration. No bare base type is allowed. A bare uuid, bytea, or timestamptz column must use its domain. Everything else, migration bookkeeping included, is a per-column exception below, and checks/spine-schema.mjs fails any exception whose introducing migration lacks the five-question justification block (format in that check's header). Adding to 'domains' or 'exceptions' is a reviewed edit to a standing permission, never a routine step.",
  "domains": [
    {
      "domain": "spine_object_id",
      "base": "uuid",
      "why": "spine object identifiers and payload keys; random by convention (0003-spine-core)"
    },
    {
      "domain": "spine_commitment",
      "base": "bytea",
      "why": "opaque cryptographic commitments to content held elsewhere (0003-spine-core)"
    },
    {
      "domain": "spine_ledger_timestamp",
      "base": "timestamp with time zone",
      "why": "ledger timestamps; checklist question 2 answered per column (0003-spine-core)"
    }
  ],
